# Contributing to {{name}}

## Setup

```bash
npm install              # installs husky hooks (commit-msg, pre-commit)
pip install pre-commit   # terraform fmt / validate / tflint / docs on commit
```

Also needed on PATH: `terraform` (version in `.terraform-version`; `tfenv` / `tenv` pick it
up automatically), [`tflint`](https://github.com/terraform-linters/tflint) and
[`terraform-docs`](https://terraform-docs.io).

## Workflow

1. Branch from `main`: `feat/<short-description>`, `fix/<short-description>`.
2. Make the change; run `terraform plan` against **dev** locally (see README).
3. Commit with [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org):
   `feat(modules): add key vault module`, `fix(terraform): correct dev address space`.
   Breaking changes: `feat!: ...` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
4. Open a PR into `main`. The CI pipeline (`.azdo/ci.yml`) runs fmt, validate, tflint and a dev plan.
5. After merge, the CD pipeline (`.azdo/cd.yml`) plans and applies dev → test → prod, pausing
   for the approvals configured on each Azure DevOps Environment.

## PR checklist

- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
- [ ] Plan output reviewed; no unexpected destroys/replacements
- [ ] New variables and outputs have descriptions (`TERRAFORM-DOCS.md` regenerated)
- [ ] No secrets in `*.tfvars` (use Key Vault references or pipeline secrets)

## Releasing

`npm run release` (`cz bump`) bumps `VERSION`, `package.json` and `CHANGELOG.md`, then tags
`vX.Y.Z`. Push with `git push --follow-tags`.
